    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **governance.test.js - \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"**\n   - **Problem**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was not being exported as a named export from `finetune/index.js`, even though the test tried to import it.\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` to maintain consistency with the module's public API.\n\n2. **eval/index.test.js - \"runs default evaluations\"**\n   - **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was accepting a second parameter (`bannedTerms`) which was being incorrectly populated with references array when called from `runEvaluations`. This caused the function to treat reference strings as toxic ban terms, flagging all outputs as toxic (score 0 instead of 1).\n   - **Fix**: Removed the `bannedTerms` parameter from the function signature so it always uses the default banned terms, regardless of what the second argument is when called by `runEvaluations`.\n\nAll 28 tests across 8 test files now pass successfully.",
